            <ArticleTitle>Henoch-Schonlein purpura associated with ranitidine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ranitidine is one of the widely prescribed H2 receptor antagonists in the treatment of peptic ulcer. It is well tolerated and has few side-effects. Vasculitic rash occurring in association with ranitidine has been described. We report a case of a 39-year-old man who developed a purpuric rash, polyarthritis, abdominal pain, melaena and impaired renal function characteristic of Henoch-Schonlein purpura, following treatment with ranitidine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
